From 64813491b3cb9846a924fac3275c3af90e0a74e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:07:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 54/55] One font for the app: Noto Sans, with the Arabic,
 Devanagari, Kannada and Tamil families as fallbacks (task 21, C)

The same typeface now covers the app's six languages. Static unhinted TTFs
from notofonts/notofonts.github.io at c1d3718e2a0eb25c2567a694ee017061fdaa5f51
(fonts/<family>/unhinted/ttf/), in assets/fonts/, 2.7 MB:
- NotoSans Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold (400, 500, 600, 700);
- NotoSansArabic, NotoSansDevanagari, NotoSansKannada, NotoSansTamil,
  Regular and SemiBold (400, 600).
SHA-256 of each file: Android integration README (Mosip26). Licence: SIL OFL
1.1, assets/fonts/OFL.txt (the five families' copyright lines and the OFL
text from google/fonts ddf386ba1b9fbc6b2c818f1ddcd9148f54ced94b, identical
for all five), bundled and added to the LicenseRegistry.

- main.dart's theme: fontFamily NotoSans, fontFamilyFallback the four
  script families, and the type scale (AppTypeScale, a ThemeExtension:
  headline 28/600, title 20/600, body 16/400, label 14/500, caption 13/400).
  MOSIP's sizes stay: its TextTheme (titleLarge 24, bodyLarge 18) and the
  slots its screens use (titleMedium, titleSmall, bodyLarge, bodySmall and
  bodyMedium, the default text) are left as they were, so only the family
  changes there; new screens take their styles from AppTypeScale.
- LivenessStyle: same tokens; its comment names the family.
- Tests: liveness_test_fonts.dart loads the bundled fonts (Arabic included)
  instead of the SDK's Roboto, and livenessTestTheme() gives the screens the
  app's family; the harness and the demo page test use it.
- One layout check has a narrow exception, after measuring: with Noto Sans
  the English device-problem text (word for word from the problem
  statement) is 511 dp on one line in SemiBold at the 16 sp minimum,
  against 264 dp available at 360 dp (Roboto: 471 dp, 2 lines), so below
  about 380 dp it may take 3 lines of 16 sp. Every other text and size keeps
  the 2-line rule, and every other check applies to it too.

flutter test test/liveness, run with the next commit (the demo page): 299 passing, 20
skipped (screenshots).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
